    {
      "name": "Inner longitudinal detrusor",
      "group": "Detrusor muscle",
      "color": "#bd5549",
      "description": "Inner longitudinal layer of the detrusor: large smooth muscle fascicles running mostly lengthways towards the bladder neck. In this dome-wall specimen the selector identifies a predominant fascicle orientation, not an independently contracting laminar sheet. Oblique bundles connect the detrusor meshwork; bladder-neck specializations are contextual and are not shown here. Preferential bundle orientation within the interlacing detrusor, not three sharply separated histologic strata.",
      "alpha": 1.0,
      "category": "muscle",
      "label": false,
