      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Middle circular detrusor",
      "group": "Detrusor muscle",
      "color": "#a8463d",
      "description": "Middle circular layer of the detrusor: the thickest layer, best defined at the bladder neck, where in males it forms the internal urethral sphincter (preventing retrograde ejaculation). In this dome-wall specimen the selector identifies a predominant fascicle orientation, not an independently contracting laminar sheet. Oblique bundles connect the detrusor meshwork; bladder-neck specializations are contextual and are not shown here. Preferential bundle orientation within the interlacing detrusor, not three sharply separated histologic strata.",
      "alpha": 1.0,
