      "group": "Detrusor muscle",
      "color": "#c46052",
      "description": "Outer longitudinal layer of the detrusor. Around the bladder neck its fibres continue into the prostate or urethral wall. In this dome-wall specimen the selector identifies a predominant fascicle orientation, not an independently contracting laminar sheet. Oblique bundles connect the detrusor meshwork; bladder-neck specializations are contextual and are not shown here. Preferential bundle orientation within the interlacing detrusor, not three sharply separated histologic strata.",
